    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d276">

                <pb facs="0360" n="240" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg240"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">033.5111 Laval, Pierre/27</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-09-24">September 24, 1931</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>During the call of the Italian Ambassador<anchor n="7" xml:id="d276-f1"/> he
                    asked me about the visit of M. Laval and whether that was going to undo all our
                    policy of disarmament. I told the Ambassador, by no means, and I spoke of the
                    good opinion I had formed of Laval during my visit to Europe and said that I
                    thought his influence was for moderation in French policy. I called the
                    Ambassador’s attention to my appointment of Wilson<anchor n="8" xml:id="d276-f2"
                    /> as a member of the Committee on the Grandi holiday proposal<anchor n="9"
                        xml:id="d276-f3"/> as evidence of my sincere desire to back them up.</p>
                <closer><signed>H[<hi rendition="#small-caps">enry</hi>] L. S[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">timson</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
